### VS Code "REST Client" extension. Start first:  python run.py
@base = http://127.0.0.1:8000

### Health
GET {{base}}/health

### Products
GET {{base}}/api/v1/products?category=electronics

### Price quote with coupon (does not change stock)
POST {{base}}/api/v1/cart/quote
Content-Type: application/json

{"items": [{"product_id": 101, "quantity": 1}, {"product_id": 104, "quantity": 1}], "coupon_code": "FEST20"}

### Place an order -> 201
POST {{base}}/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer_email": "priya@example.com",
  "address": {"name": "Priya Sharma", "city": "Bengaluru", "pincode": "560001", "phone": "9876543210"},
  "items": [{"product_id": 101, "quantity": 2}],
  "coupon_code": "WELCOME10"
}

### Track the order (use the order_id you got above)
GET {{base}}/api/v1/orders/SK-1001

### Out of stock -> 409
POST {{base}}/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer_email": "rahul@example.com",
  "address": {"name": "Rahul", "city": "Pune", "pincode": "411001", "phone": "9123456780"},
  "items": [{"product_id": 103, "quantity": 1}]
}

### Bad data -> 422
POST {{base}}/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"customer_email": "not-an-email", "address": {"name": "R", "city": "Pune", "pincode": "0123", "phone": "12345"}, "items": []}
